import lib/font.dl
import lib/ui_geometry.dl

class:
    patterns:
        linear UI paint
    members:
        red as a 32 bit floating-point number
        green as a 32 bit floating-point number
        blue as a 32 bit floating-point number

to get the UI [corner point] {integer:index} of {integer:steps} on {UI bounds:box} rounded by {floating-point number:radius} expanded by {floating-point number:fringe}:
    set corner to index / steps
    set step to index mod steps
    set angle to (((corner * 90) + 180) as a floating-point number) + ((step as a floating-point number) * (90.0 / ((steps - 1) as a floating-point number)))
    set radians to angle * 0.017453292519943295
    set centerX to (box's x as a floating-point number) + radius
    set centerY to (box's y as a floating-point number) + radius
    if corner = 1 or corner = 2:
        set centerX to ((box's x + box's width) as a floating-point number) - radius
    if corner = 2 or corner = 3:
        set centerY to ((box's y + box's height) as a floating-point number) - radius
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI point, centerX + (the cosine of radians) * (radius + fringe), centerY + (the sine of radians) * (radius + fringe))

to get the linear UI [ink] of {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set state to frame's window as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    return @intrinsic("construct", linear UI paint, graphics color channel (ink's red) for state, graphics color channel (ink's green) for state, graphics color channel (ink's blue) for state)

to get linear UI ink between {linear UI paint:first} and {linear UI paint:second} at {floating-point number:amount}:
    set phase to (the minimum of 1.0 and (the maximum of 0.0 and amount)) as a 32 bit floating-point number
    set red to first's red + ((second's red - first's red) * phase)
    set green to first's green + ((second's green - first's green) * phase)
    set blue to first's blue + ((second's blue - first's blue) * phase)
    return @intrinsic("construct", linear UI paint, red, green, blue)

to add UI vertex {UI point:point} in {linear UI paint:ink} with alpha {integer:alpha} to {graphics frame:frame}:
    set state to frame's window as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set state's current_vertex's color to [ink's red, ink's green, ink's blue, (alpha as a 32 bit floating-point number) / (255.0 as a 32 bit floating-point number)]
    add a vertex at x point's x and y point's y to frame

to draw a rounded UI box {UI bounds:box} with radius {floating-point number:radius} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    draw a rounded UI surface box with radius radius from ink to ink opacity 255 feathered by 0.75 on frame

to add UI vertex {UI point:point} shaded from {linear UI paint:top} to {linear UI paint:bottom} across {UI bounds:box} with alpha {integer:alpha} to {graphics frame:frame}:
    set amount to (point's y - box's y) / box's height
    add UI vertex point in (linear UI ink between top and bottom at amount) with alpha alpha to frame

# Geometry carries a gradient and coverage; the same primitive draws crisp
# surfaces and wide, translucent shadow fringes at fractional coordinates.
to draw a rounded UI surface {UI bounds:box} with radius {floating-point number:radius} from {UI paint:top} to {UI paint:bottom} opacity {integer:opacity} feathered by {floating-point number:feather} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    if frame's drawable:
        set upper to the linear UI ink of top on frame
        set lower to the linear UI ink of bottom on frame
        set rounding to radius
        set limit to (box's width as a floating-point number) / 2.0
        if box's height < box's width:
            set limit to (box's height as a floating-point number) / 2.0
        if rounding > limit:
            set rounding to limit
        set center to @intrinsic("construct", UI point, (box's x as a floating-point number) + (box's width as a floating-point number) / 2.0, (box's y as a floating-point number) + (box's height as a floating-point number) / 2.0)
        set steps to the maximum of 5 and (((the square root of (rounding * 2.0)) as an integer) + 3)
        set count to steps * 4
        start triangles in frame
        set index to 0
        loop while index < count:
            set next to (index + 1) mod count
            set insideA to the UI corner point index of steps on box rounded by rounding expanded by -0.5
            set insideB to the UI corner point next of steps on box rounded by rounding expanded by -0.5
            set outsideA to the UI corner point index of steps on box rounded by rounding expanded by feather
            set outsideB to the UI corner point next of steps on box rounded by rounding expanded by feather
            add UI vertex center shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex insideA shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex insideB shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex insideA shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex insideB shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex outsideB shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha 0 to frame
            add UI vertex insideA shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha opacity to frame
            add UI vertex outsideB shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha 0 to frame
            add UI vertex outsideA shaded from upper to lower across box with alpha 0 to frame
            increment index
        finish triangles in frame
        set graphics vertex color to red 255 green 255 blue 255 alpha 255 in (frame's window as a pointer to DynlexGraphics)

to draw a UI [shadow] under {UI bounds:box} with radius {floating-point number:radius} softness {floating-point number:softness} strength {integer:strength} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set shadow to UI box at (box's x) (box's y + 6.0) sized (box's width) (box's height)
    draw a rounded UI surface shadow with radius radius from ink to ink opacity strength feathered by softness on frame

to draw a UI disc at {UI point:center} with radius {floating-point number:radius} from {UI paint:top} to {UI paint:bottom} opacity {integer:opacity} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set box to UI box at (center's x - radius) (center's y - radius) sized (radius * 2.0) (radius * 2.0)
    draw a rounded UI surface box with radius radius from top to bottom opacity opacity feathered by 0.75 on frame

to draw a glass UI panel {UI bounds:box} with radius {floating-point number:radius} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    draw a UI shadow under box with radius radius softness 12.0 strength 32 in (UI ink 0 0 0) on frame
    set rim to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 164 196 221) at 0.12
    set edge to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 2 8 16) at 0.18
    draw a rounded UI surface box with radius radius from rim to edge opacity 255 feathered by 0.75 on frame
    set inside to UI box at (box's x + 1.0) (box's y + 1.0) sized (box's width - 2.0) (box's height - 2.0)
    set top to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 129 160 187) at 0.035
    set bottom to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 2 8 18) at 0.1
    draw a rounded UI surface inside with radius (radius - 1.0) from top to bottom opacity 255 feathered by 0.5 on frame
    set reflection to UI box at (box's x + radius) (box's y + 1.0) sized (box's width - (2.0 * radius)) 0.8
    draw a rounded UI surface reflection with radius 0.4 from (UI ink 211 232 245) to (UI ink 211 232 245) opacity 10 feathered by 0.5 on frame

to draw a flat UI box {UI bounds:box} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    draw a rectangle at x box's x and y box's y with width box's width and height box's height in color red ink's red, green ink's green and blue ink's blue in frame

to draw UI text {a value:message} at {a value:x} {a value:y} with {font:typeface} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set rendering to the result of drawing message as text at x x and y y using typeface in color red ink's red, green ink's green and blue ink's blue in frame
    require condition (rendering succeeded) reporting "Rendering UI text failed"

to draw UI text {a value:message} centered in {UI bounds:box} with {font:typeface} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set width to the width of message using typeface
    draw UI text message at (box's x + (box's width - width) / 2) (box's y + ((box's height / 2) + 5)) with typeface in ink on frame

to draw a UI stroke from {UI point:first} to {UI point:second} with width {floating-point number:width} from {UI paint:first ink} to {UI paint:second ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    draw a UI stroke from first to second with width width opacity 255 from first ink to second ink on frame

to get the shaded UI color of {UI paint:ink} at {floating-point number:side} across {UI point:normal}:
    set illumination to 0.5 - (side * ((normal's x * 0.3) + (normal's y * 0.5)))
    set shine to (1.0 - side * side) * 0.2
    set dark to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 5 39 48) at 0.3
    set light to UI ink between ink and (UI ink 234 255 251) at 0.28
    return UI ink between dark and light at (illumination + shine)

to draw a glossy UI stroke from {UI point:first} to {UI point:second} with width {floating-point number:width} from {UI paint:first ink} to {UI paint:second ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set horizontal to second's x - first's x
    set vertical to second's y - first's y
    set distance to the square root of ((horizontal * horizontal) + (vertical * vertical))
    if distance > 0.0:
        set normal to a UI point at (-vertical / distance) and (horizontal / distance)
        set layers to [-1.0, -0.45, 0.2, 1.0]
        start triangles in frame
        set index to 0
        loop while index < 3:
            set {first side} to the item at index in layers
            set {second side} to the item at (index + 1) in layers
            set {first offset} to (first side * width) / 2.0
            set {second offset} to (second side * width) / 2.0
            set {first A} to a UI point at (first's x + normal's x * first offset) and (first's y + normal's y * first offset)
            set {first B} to a UI point at (first's x + normal's x * second offset) and (first's y + normal's y * second offset)
            set {second A} to a UI point at (second's x + normal's x * first offset) and (second's y + normal's y * first offset)
            set {second B} to a UI point at (second's x + normal's x * second offset) and (second's y + normal's y * second offset)
            set {first light} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of first ink at first side across normal) on frame
            set {first dark} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of first ink at second side across normal) on frame
            set {second light} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of second ink at first side across normal) on frame
            set {second dark} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of second ink at second side across normal) on frame
            add UI vertex first A in first light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second A in second light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second B in second dark with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex first A in first light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second B in second dark with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex first B in first dark with alpha 255 to frame
            increment index
        set side to -1.0
        loop while side <= 1.0:
            set inside to (side * width) / 2.0
            set outside to side * (width / 2.0 + 0.9)
            set {first A} to a UI point at (first's x + normal's x * inside) and (first's y + normal's y * inside)
            set {first B} to a UI point at (first's x + normal's x * outside) and (first's y + normal's y * outside)
            set {second A} to a UI point at (second's x + normal's x * inside) and (second's y + normal's y * inside)
            set {second B} to a UI point at (second's x + normal's x * outside) and (second's y + normal's y * outside)
            set {first light} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of first ink at side across normal) on frame
            set {second light} to the linear UI ink of (the shaded UI color of second ink at side across normal) on frame
            add UI vertex first A in first light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second A in second light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second B in second light with alpha 0 to frame
            add UI vertex first A in first light with alpha 255 to frame
            add UI vertex second B in second light with alpha 0 to frame
            add UI vertex first B in first light with alpha 0 to frame
            set side to side + 2.0
        finish triangles in frame
        use vertex color red 255, green 255 and blue 255 in frame

to draw a UI stroke from {UI point:first} to {UI point:second} with width {floating-point number:width} opacity {integer:opacity} from {UI paint:first ink} to {UI paint:second ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    if (first's x = second's x) and (first's y = second's y):
        return nothing
    set {first paint} to the linear UI ink of first ink on frame
    set {second paint} to the linear UI ink of second ink on frame
    start triangles in frame
    append a UI stroke from first to second with width width opacity opacity from first paint to second paint on frame
    finish triangles in frame
    use vertex color red 255, green 255 and blue 255 in frame

to append a UI stroke from {UI point:first} to {UI point:second} with width {floating-point number:width} opacity {integer:opacity} from {linear UI paint:first paint} to {linear UI paint:second paint} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set horizontal to second's x - first's x
    set vertical to second's y - first's y
    set distance to the square root of ((horizontal * horizontal) + (vertical * vertical))
    if distance > 0.0:
        set across to (((vertical / distance) * width) / 2.0)
        set along to (((horizontal / distance) * width) / 2.0)
        set {first A} to a UI point at (first's x - across) and (first's y + along)
        set {first B} to a UI point at (first's x + across) and (first's y - along)
        set {second A} to a UI point at (second's x - across) and (second's y + along)
        set {second B} to a UI point at (second's x + across) and (second's y - along)
        add UI vertex first A in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second A in second paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second B in second paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex first A in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second B in second paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex first B in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        set across to (vertical / distance) * (width / 2.0 + 0.9)
        set along to (horizontal / distance) * (width / 2.0 + 0.9)
        set {first outside A} to a UI point at (first's x - across) and (first's y + along)
        set {first outside B} to a UI point at (first's x + across) and (first's y - along)
        set {second outside A} to a UI point at (second's x - across) and (second's y + along)
        set {second outside B} to a UI point at (second's x + across) and (second's y - along)
        add UI vertex first A in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second A in second paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second outside A in second paint with alpha 0 to frame
        add UI vertex first A in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second outside A in second paint with alpha 0 to frame
        add UI vertex first outside A in first paint with alpha 0 to frame
        add UI vertex first B in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second B in second paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second outside B in second paint with alpha 0 to frame
        add UI vertex first B in first paint with alpha opacity to frame
        add UI vertex second outside B in second paint with alpha 0 to frame
        add UI vertex first outside B in first paint with alpha 0 to frame
